    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n7998" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cĭlĭum</span></b> , ii,
			n.
		kindr. with Gr. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κυλίς,
		κύλα</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>An eyelid</i>, Paul. ex <i><span class="en">Fest. p.
				43, 3</span></i> Müll.; <i><span class="en">Plin. 11,
				39, 93, § 227</span></i>; <i><span class="en">App. M.
				10, p. 247, 10</span></i>; Lact. Opif. Dei, 10 <i>init.</i>—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>the lower
			eyelid</i> (opp. supercilium): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">extremum ambitum genae superioris,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					11, 37, 57, § 157</span></i>
			.</div>
